		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=24196#p24196"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Hello,</p><br /><p>You can also consider sending question on pgsql-general mailing list (<a href="https://www.postgresql.org/list/" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/list/</a>).</p><br /><p>Anyway, your problem is that you tell your server where to put the socket file, but you don&#039;t tell your client it was moved. So without any further instruction, it just fallbacks to default location in /var.</p><br /><p>You can run &quot;psql -h /tmp&quot;, or put in your .bashrc file or similar a </p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>export PGHOST=&quot;/tmp&quot;</code></pre></div><br /><p>Regards.</p>]]></content>
